<section class="ph"><div class="ph-media"><img class="ph-img" src="/assets/img/photos/storm-sky.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/storm-sky-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/storm-sky.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap ph-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><a href="/mi-cities-served/">Cities</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span aria-current="page">Flint</span></nav><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Mid-Michigan · Genesee County</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Flint, Michigan</h1><p class="ph-lede">Flint’s neighborhoods grew up around the auto plants, and many of its homes date from that boom: solid, modest houses in Civic Park, grander ones in the College Cultural area. The city also carries the memory of one of the deadliest tornadoes in American history.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-maize" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-glass" href="/request-claim-review/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="ph-facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Genesee County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Mid-Michigan</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<div class="local"><div><p class="local-k">Neighborhoods &amp; areas</p><p>Carriage Town, Civic Park, Mott Park, College Cultural, Woodcroft Estates, Grand Traverse District, Downtown, nearby Beecher</p></div><div><p class="local-k">Housing mix</p><p>Flint has a large stock of 1910s–1950s wood-frame and brick homes built for auto workers, larger period homes near the cultural center, and postwar suburbs in surrounding Genesee County townships.</p></div><div><p class="local-k">Common claim drivers</p><ul class="chips"><li>Tornado and wind</li><li>Fire and smoke</li><li>Frozen pipes</li><li>Basement water</li><li>Hail damage</li></ul></div></div>
<h2>Flint and Genesee County: Getting a Fair Number on Your Claim</h2>
<p>Flint homeowners know resilience. The city’s housing was largely built during the auto industry’s rise, and many of those homes are now a century old. They were built well, but age brings its own claim challenges: knob-and-tube or older wiring that complicates fire repairs, original plumbing that freezes in a hard winter, and roofs that have been layered over more than once.</p>
<h3>The 1953 Flint–Beecher tornado</h3>
<p>On June 8, 1953, a violent tornado struck the Beecher area just north of Flint, causing catastrophic damage and great loss of life. It remains one of the deadliest tornadoes in United States history. The storm reshaped how Michigan approached severe weather warnings, and it is a reminder that Genesee County sits squarely in the path of spring and summer storm systems moving across the Lower Peninsula. Today, wind and hail claims are a regular part of life in Flint, Burton, Grand Blanc and the surrounding townships.</p>
<h3>Older homes and fire losses</h3>
<p>Fire and smoke claims in older homes are often among the hardest to settle. Smoke travels through balloon-framed walls and into attics, and odor can linger long after visible soot is cleaned. An insurer’s estimate may cover cleaning where replacement is needed, or leave out contents entirely. In Civic Park, Mott Park and Carriage Town, where homes have original woodwork and plaster, the gap between a quick estimate and a real restoration scope can be wide. Our <a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/fire-smoke-loss-appraisal/">fire and smoke loss appraisal</a> service reviews every line, from structure to contents.</p>
<h3>Rental properties and vacancy</h3>
<p>Many Flint homes are rentals, and landlords face issues that owner-occupants don’t: tenant-reported losses that arrive late, vacancy provisions that can limit coverage, and disputes about pre-existing conditions. Appraisal can resolve disagreements about the amount of a covered loss, but questions about vacancy exclusions or late notice belong with a Michigan attorney.</p>
<p>Winter brings its own problems to Flint’s older homes. Plumbing on exterior walls, unheated crawl spaces and vacant neighboring houses can all contribute to frozen and burst pipes during deep cold, such as the late-January 2019 polar vortex. These water claims often turn on how much drying, demolition and rebuilding the damage truly requires.</p>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Contents count too</b>After a fire, personal property often makes up a large share of the loss. A room-by-room inventory, with photos and receipts where you have them, makes any contents dispute easier to resolve.</div>
<p>If contents are part of your dispute, see our <a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/contents-personal-property-appraisal/">contents and personal property appraisal</a> service. You can also check how prepared you are with the <a href="/mi-claim-calculators/appraisal-readiness-score/">appraisal readiness score</a>.</p>
<h2>Services available in Flint</h2>
<p>Every Michigan Insurance Appraiser service is available to owners in Flint and surrounding communities, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Demand Representation</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/homeowner-claim-appraiser/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/commercial-condo-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial, Condo &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/hail-roof-damage-appraisal/">Hail &amp; Roof Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/windstorm-tornado-appraisal/">Windstorm &amp; Tornado Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/ice-dam-frozen-pipe-appraisal/">Ice Dam &amp; Frozen Pipe Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/water-sewer-backup-appraisal/">Water &amp; Sewer Backup Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/fire-smoke-loss-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Loss Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Questions from Flint property owners</h2><div class="qa"><details><summary><span>Can appraisal help with a smoke damage dispute in Flint?</span><i class="qa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>Yes, if the insurer agrees the fire is covered and the disagreement is about how much it costs to clean, repair or replace. Appraisal is designed for exactly that kind of amount-of-loss dispute.</p></div></details><details><summary><span>Do you cover Burton, Grand Blanc and Flint Township?</span><i class="qa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>Yes. We work throughout Genesee County and the rest of Michigan.</p></div></details><details><summary><span>How much does appraisal cost?</span><i class="qa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>Each side generally pays its own appraiser and shares the umpire’s cost, though policy wording varies. We’ll explain our fee structure before you commit to anything.</p></div></details></div>
